<title>AUSTRALIA: Rugby union-Hardy scores twice in dream Australia debut.</title>
<headline>Rugby union-Hardy scores twice in dream Australia debut.</headline>
<byline>Robert Galvin</byline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-06-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Winger Mitch Hardy lifted Australia to a convincing 29-15 win against France in the first rugby union test with two tries in a brief but memorable test debut on Saturday.</p>
<p>The ACT Brumbies winger transformed the match during a 12-minute stint during the second half at the Sydney Football Stadium as a temporary replacement for full-back Stephen Larkham.</p>
</text>
